# Advisory session indicator

Branch: `session-indicator`, based on current root main
`5593932d5e8bc9fea2f52292fc0a5665b5c650a0` and Client main
`b5c3a7a5ddd37e010155883054931be3010fc5a2` (1.1.014).
Integrates root PR13, Client PR8 and Linux Host PR10 without replacing the
newer native camera, stereo microphone or audio-clock work.

## Contract

- Show In Session for a logged-in local desktop or reserved/live PLANK stream.
- Advisory only: same-user local-to-remote access, explicit remote takeover and
  different-user ownership enforcement are unchanged.
- Optional Linux username publication remains administrator-controlled and off
  by default. Opt-in exposes the sanitized name before authentication.
- No extra poll, account lookup, auth queue work or teardown from discovery.
- No persistent usernames in Client bookmarks. Preserve readable status while
  truncating long names. macOS publishes only nameless occupancy.

## Implementation

1. Retain the PR Client model/parser/UI work on top of current Client main.
   Reject names unless occupancy is exactly1; preserve the status label width.
2. Reuse the account already resolved by the Linux supervisor. Bind its sanitized
   advisory name to the versioned private attachment record, and confirm the same
   UID/session/class against local logind before returning it. No new resolver,
   polling thread or service. Read stream occupancy atomically instead of calling
   the cleanup-producing session_count function.
3. Reflect macOS pending/active stream leases through an atomic advisory bit.
   Select pre-serialized occupied/free responses on the network queue; retain
   existing authentication and ownership policy without new locks or OS queries.
4. Test parser limits, privacy default, scope loss, login-screen streams, lease
   expiry/revocation, persistence absence and unchanged authentication behavior.
5. Run focused Linux and SDK27 checks from exact-source worktrees. Package builds
   and live desktop/takeover/UI acceptance remain separate gates. No deployment,
   release or merge to main without the corresponding operator request.

## Validation

Linux production occupancy and private-record tests pass locally, including
10000 cached reads, name limits, malformed records and desktop transitions.
Existing session-policy tests pass. SDK27 auth/discovery and Qt Client parser
qualification are pending. Full package and live session qualification pending.
